{
"nodes":[
{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"# Parkinson's Disease — Multi-Agent Pathway Discovery\n**Input:** disease name → **Output:** explained, cited report of candidate pathways (genes · proteins · mechanisms)\n\n⚠ 'Breakthrough' here = a *simulated*, in-silico hypothesis. Never a clinical claim.","x":-520,"y":-780,"width":1000,"height":150},
{"id":"count","type":"text","text":"## How many agents?\n**10 agents = 1 Orchestrator + 9 workers**\n- 4 collectors, one tool each: Disease–Gene · PPI · Pathway · Literature\n- 2 graph agents: Builder · Ranker\n- 3 reasoning agents: Hypothesis · Critic · Report\n\n**+ 1 Evaluation Harness** (deterministic, not an LLM agent)\n\nMVP cut (8 agents): merge Builder+Ranker and Critic+Report.","x":600,"y":-780,"width":600,"height":300},
{"id":"input","type":"text","text":"## INPUT\nDisease name: **'Parkinson disease'**","x":-270,"y":-600,"width":500,"height":80,"color":"5"},
{"id":"orch","type":"text","text":"# AGENT 0 — ORCHESTRATOR (supervisor)\n- Parse disease name → resolve ontology IDs (EFO_0002508 / MONDO_0005180)\n- Plan and dispatch Layer 1 agents **in parallel**\n- Own the shared state; enforce gates; retry or fall back to cache\n- Control the Critic ↔ Hypothesis revision loop (max 2)\n- Budget guard: LLM tokens, API rate limits\n- Switch between **RUN mode** and **EVAL mode**","x":-370,"y":-480,"width":700,"height":290,"color":"1"},
{"id":"state","type":"text","text":"# Shared State & Cache\n(LangGraph state + disk cache)\n- disease IDs, seed genes\n- raw tool outputs (versioned)\n- graph file, ranked list\n- hypotheses, critic verdicts\n- run log for reproducibility","x":-1340,"y":-480,"width":380,"height":290},
{"id":"g1","type":"group","label":"LAYER 1 — KNOWLEDGE COLLECTION (4 agents, parallel)","x":-900,"y":-130,"width":1760,"height":400,"color":"4"},
{"id":"a1","type":"text","text":"# A1 — Disease–Gene Agent\n**Tool:** Open Targets Platform (GraphQL)\n**In:** disease ID\n**Out:** ranked targets, association score, evidence types (genetics, literature, animal models…)\n**PD seeds (examples):** SNCA, LRRK2, GBA1, PRKN, PINK1, PARK7","x":-860,"y":-80,"width":400,"height":320,"color":"4"},
{"id":"a2","type":"text","text":"# A2 — Protein Interaction Agent\n**Tool:** STRING API\n**In:** seed + top genes\n**Out:** weighted PPI edges (confidence threshold), 1st and 2nd-shell neighbours\n**Risk:** hub bias; STRING text-mining edges overlap with PubMed (circularity)","x":-430,"y":-80,"width":400,"height":320,"color":"4"},
{"id":"a3","type":"text","text":"# A3 — Pathway Agent\n**Tools:** Reactome + KEGG (e.g. hsa05012 Parkinson disease)\n**In:** gene list\n**Out:** gene → pathway membership, pathway hierarchy, known PD pathways (= ground truth for evaluation)\n**Risk:** Reactome ↔ KEGG ID/name mismatch; KEGG licence = academic use","x":0,"y":-80,"width":400,"height":320,"color":"4"},
{"id":"a4","type":"text","text":"# A4 — Literature Agent\n**Tool:** PubMed (E-utilities)\n**In:** disease + gene/pathway terms\n**Out:** PMIDs, abstracts, publication year, gene–mechanism co-mentions\n**Also:** answers follow-up queries from the Critic\n**Risk:** must honour the temporal cutoff in EVAL mode","x":430,"y":-80,"width":400,"height":320,"color":"4"},
{"id":"gate1","type":"text","text":"**GATE 1 — Data QC**\nAll sources returned? ID-mapping coverage OK? Otherwise retry / use cache.","x":-370,"y":330,"width":700,"height":90,"color":"3"},
{"id":"g2","type":"group","label":"LAYER 2 — GRAPH CONSTRUCTION & REASONING (2 agents)","x":-410,"y":470,"width":780,"height":750,"color":"2"},
{"id":"a5","type":"text","text":"# A5 — Graph Builder Agent\n**Tool:** NetworkX\n- Normalise IDs (HGNC / Ensembl / UniProt)\n- Node types: Disease · Gene/Protein · Pathway · Mechanism · Paper\n- Edge types: associated_with · interacts_with · member_of · mentioned_in\n- Weight = source confidence; **provenance on every edge** (source, score, PMID)\n**Out:** one unified knowledge graph","x":-370,"y":520,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"2"},
{"id":"a6","type":"text","text":"# A6 — Graph Ranker Agent\n**Tools:** NetworkX / graph-ML libraries\n1. Shortest paths: Disease → candidate → Pathway\n2. Random walk with restart from PD seeds\n3. Link prediction (Adamic–Adar, Jaccard, node embeddings)\n4. Fuse scores; remove already-known links; correct hub bias\n**Out:** ranked candidate genes / pathways / mechanisms + supporting paths","x":-370,"y":850,"width":700,"height":330,"color":"2"},
{"id":"gate2","type":"text","text":"**GATE 2 — Ranking sanity**\nNot only hub genes? Known links excluded from the 'novel' list? Enough supporting paths per candidate?","x":-370,"y":1270,"width":700,"height":90,"color":"3"},
{"id":"g3","type":"group","label":"LAYER 3 — HYPOTHESIS, VERIFICATION & REPORT (3 agents)","x":-410,"y":1410,"width":780,"height":940,"color":"6"},
{"id":"a7","type":"text","text":"# A7 — Hypothesis Generator Agent\n**Tool:** LLM API\n**In:** top-k candidates + graph paths + abstracts\n**Out:** structured hypothesis cards: proposed chain (gene → protein → pathway → PD phenotype), rationale, testable prediction, evidence IDs","x":-370,"y":1460,"width":700,"height":220,"color":"6"},
{"id":"a8","type":"text","text":"# A8 — Evidence Critic Agent\n**Tools:** LLM + PubMed lookup\n- Does every claim have a citation (PMID / DB record)?\n- Does the cited text really support it?\n- Novelty check vs known links; contradictions flagged\n- Verdict: accept / revise / need more evidence\n**Loop:** revise → A7 (max 2) · evidence gap → A4 via Orchestrator","x":-370,"y":1730,"width":700,"height":300,"color":"6"},
{"id":"a9","type":"text","text":"# A9 — Report Writer Agent\n**Tool:** LLM + graph plotting\n**Out:** explained report: ranked hypotheses, evidence table with citations, path figures, confidence, limitations, and the label **'SIMULATED BREAKTHROUGH — in-silico hypothesis'**","x":-370,"y":2080,"width":700,"height":230,"color":"6"},
{"id":"output","type":"text","text":"## OUTPUT\nExplained report + candidate-pathway graph (cited, with reproducible run log)","x":-270,"y":2400,"width":500,"height":90,"color":"5"},
{"id":"eval","type":"text","text":"# EVALUATION HARNESS\n(non-LLM · runs when Orchestrator is in EVAL mode)\n1. **Hide** k% of known disease/gene → pathway links (A3 ground truth)\n2. **Temporal cutoff:** PubMed / Open Targets data only up to year Y\n3. **Re-run** A1 → A8 on the masked data\n4. **Score:** Recall@k, Hits@10, MRR, AUROC / AUPRC\n5. **Baselines:** random, degree, shortest-path only\n6. **Ablations:** drop each agent / tool\n7. **Leakage audit:** hidden links absent from STRING, literature and graph","x":1000,"y":500,"width":600,"height":780,"color":"#7a7a7a"},
{"id":"sim","type":"text","text":"# SIMULATED BREAKTHROUGH SCENARIO\nHide a well-established PD mechanism (e.g. PINK1/PRKN mitophagy or the GBA1–lysosome link) and apply a temporal cutoff.\n\n**Counts as a simulated breakthrough if:**\n- the hidden mechanism re-appears in the top-k, AND\n- at least one novel cross-talk hypothesis passes the Critic with verified citations\n\nAlways reported as an in-silico hypothesis needing lab validation.","x":1000,"y":1340,"width":600,"height":360,"color":"6"},
{"id":"legend","type":"text","text":"# Legend\n🔴 Orchestrator\n🟢 Collector agents\n🟠 Graph agents\n🟣 LLM reasoning agents\n🟡 Quality gates\n🔵 Input / Output\n⚪ Evaluation harness","x":-1340,"y":2100,"width":380,"height":240}
],
